x names everything else. Expand a subtree when its narration (or name) shows your subject plausibly lives there — you'll get the trajectory, the variants, and the verbatim witness. But be strict about absence: if neither the map's narrations nor the index's names substantively cover your subject, it is NOT in this perspective — say so rather than expanding a loose thematic match (a word-overlap is not coverage). Decide from the map; expand to ground.\n\n# The map (steering grain)\n\n\n# Focus: document review, first version, reviewer metadata (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n","positions":"","pin":"58d5e4fbcce789f426dbb8efcbcb4e0059d06284","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":1840},"live_run_id":"d08c47bfa67c","at":"2026-07-21T10:03:15Z"}
